          "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued November 11 at 12:14AM PST until November 13 at 6:00PM PST by NWS San Francisco CA",
          "severity": "Moderate",
          "urgency": "Expected",
          "description": "* WHAT...For the Beach Hazards Statement, An increased risk for\nsneaker waves and strong rip currents with breaking waves of 15\nto 20 ft expected. For the High Surf Warning, Dangerously large\nbreaking waves of 25 to 30 ft expected.\n\n* WHERE...Coastal North Bay Including Point Reyes National\nSeashore, San Francisco Peninsula Coast and Northern Monterey\nBay Counties.\n\n* WHEN...For the Beach Hazards Statement, from 9 PM Wednesday\nthrough 6 PM Friday. For the High Surf Warning, from 6 PM Friday\nto 4 AM Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Dangerously large breaking waves can overpower\nswimmers, pulling people into the sea from beaches, jetties, and\nrocks resulting in significant physical injury and increasing\nthe risk of drowning. Waves can sweep across the shoreline\nwithout warning, pulling people into the sea from beaches,\njetties, and rocks.",
          "instruction": "Everyone should remain out of the water due to life-threatening\nsurf conditions. Stay off of jetties, piers, and other waterside\ninfrastructure.\n\nStay off of jetties, piers, rocks, and other waterside\ninfrastructure. Remain out of the water to avoid hazardous surf\nand NEVER turn your back on the ocean. Monitor local weather,\nsurf and tide forecasts at www.weather.gov/mtr.",
